  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Assessing barriers, motivators, and youth political participation in Namibia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The purpose of this project is to generate comprehensive qualitative research findings on youth political participation in Namibia, aimed at addressing the significant challenge of youth disengagement from democratic processes. By understanding the barriers and motivators affecting young Namibians&apos; engagement in electoral activities, the project seeks to empower youth with the knowledge and tools necessary to participate meaningfully in the upcoming 2025 regional council and local authority elections. Ultimately, the initiative aims to promote a more inclusive and resilient democratic system in Namibia by promoting informed civic activism and facilitating greater youth involvement in political decision-making. The project aims: Identify the key barriers to youth political participation; Understand the motivators for youth political participation; Provide evidence-based insights for developing future youth engagement strategies; Facilitate youth-led discussions on political participation.</narrative>
  </description>
